---
/**
 * Keep unmatched requests inside Astro's router instead of the Vercel
 * adapter's forced-status catch-all.
 *
 * Localized URLs are intentionally not duplicated as page files. Middleware
 * rewrites `/es/bible/...` to the shared `/bible/...` route, but Vercel must
 * first dispatch the original nested path to Astro without pre-setting a 404
 * status. This rest route gives the adapter that dispatch target. Anything the
 * locale rewrite does not recognize still reaches the canonical 404 page and
 * receives its explicit status, cache policy and noindex directive.
 */
return Astro.rewrite('/404');
